#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Using-ros2-param.rst:13
msgid "Using the ``ros2 param`` command-line tool — how-to"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Using-ros2-param.rst:16
msgid ""
"Parameters let you inspect and adjust node configuration while a ROS system "
"is running. This article describes how to use the ``ros2 param`` command-"
"line tool to list, get, set, delete, describe, dump, and load parameters. "
"After you follow these steps, you will be able to manage node parameters "
"from the command line."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Using-ros2-param.rst:26
msgid "Table of Contents"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Using-ros2-param.rst:28
msgid ""
"Parameters in ROS 2 can be get, set, listed, and described through a set of "
"services as described in :doc:`the concept document <../../About-"
"Parameters>`. The ``ros2 param`` command-line tool is a wrapper around these "
"service calls that makes it easy to manipulate parameters from the command-"
"line."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Using-ros2-param.rst:32
msgid "Summary"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Using-ros2-param.rst:34
msgid ""
"The ``ros2 param`` command-line tool wraps parameter service calls so you "
"can manage node parameters without writing code."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Using-ros2-param.rst:36
msgid "Use it to:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Using-ros2-param.rst:38
msgid ""
"List parameters on one node or all discoverable nodes with ``ros2 param "
"list``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Using-ros2-param.rst:39
msgid "Get or set values with ``ros2 param get`` and ``ros2 param set``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Using-ros2-param.rst:40
msgid "Delete only dynamic parameters with ``ros2 param`` delete."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Using-ros2-param.rst:41
msgid ""
"Describe, dump, and load parameters with ``ros2 param describe``, ``ros2 "
"param dump``, and ``ros2 param load``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Using-ros2-param.rst:43
msgid ""
"Values passed to ``ros2 param set`` use YAML syntax, so explicitly mark "
"strings such as ``!!str off`` when needed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Using-ros2-param.rst:46
msgid "``ros2 param list``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Using-ros2-param.rst:48
msgid ""
"This command will list all of the available parameters on a given node, or "
"on all discoverable nodes if no node is given."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Using-ros2-param.rst:50
msgid "To get all of the parameters on a given node:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Using-ros2-param.rst:52
msgid "$ ros2 param list /my_node"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Using-ros2-param.rst:56
msgid ""
"To get all of the parameters on all nodes in the system (this can take a "
"long time on a complicated network):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Using-ros2-param.rst:58
msgid "$ ros2 param list"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Using-ros2-param.rst:63
msgid "``ros2 param get``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Using-ros2-param.rst:65
msgid ""
"This command will get the value of a particular parameter. It can query a "
"specific node or search across all nodes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Using-ros2-param.rst:68
msgid "To get the value of a parameter across all nodes:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Using-ros2-param.rst:70
msgid "$ ros2 param get use_sim_time"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Using-ros2-param.rst:74
msgid ""
"This will display the parameter value for each node that has this parameter "
"set."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Using-ros2-param.rst:76
msgid "To get the value of a parameter on a specific node:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Using-ros2-param.rst:78
msgid "$ ros2 param get /my_node use_sim_time"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Using-ros2-param.rst:83
msgid "``ros2 param set``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Using-ros2-param.rst:85
msgid ""
"This command will set the value of a particular parameter on a particular "
"node. For most parameters, the type of the new value must be the same as the "
"existing type."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Using-ros2-param.rst:88
msgid "To set the value of a parameter on a node:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Using-ros2-param.rst:90
msgid "$ ros2 param set /my_node use_sim_time false"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Using-ros2-param.rst:94
msgid ""
"The value that is passed on the command-line is in YAML, which allows "
"arbitrary YAML expressions to be used. However, it also means that certain "
"expressions will be interpreted differently than might be expected. For "
"instance, if the parameter ``my_string`` on node ``my_node`` is of type "
"string, the following will not work:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Using-ros2-param.rst:98
msgid "$ ros2 param set /my_node my_string off"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Using-ros2-param.rst:102
msgid ""
"That's because YAML is interpreting \"off\" as a boolean, and ``my_string`` "
"is a string type. This can be worked around by using the YAML syntax for "
"explicitly setting strings, e.g.:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Using-ros2-param.rst:105
msgid "$ ros param set /my_node my_string '!!str off'"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Using-ros2-param.rst:109
msgid ""
"Additionally, YAML supports heterogeneous lists, containing (say) a string, "
"a boolean, and an integer. However, ROS 2 parameters do not support "
"heterogeneous lists, so any YAML list that has multiple types will be "
"interpreted as a string. Assuming that the parameter ``my_int_array`` on "
"node ``my_node`` is of type integer array, the following will not work:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Using-ros2-param.rst:113
msgid "$ ros param set /my_node my_int_array '[foo,off,1]'"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Using-ros2-param.rst:117
msgid "The following string typed parameter would work:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Using-ros2-param.rst:119
msgid "$ ros param set /my_node my_string '[foo,off,1]'"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Using-ros2-param.rst:124
msgid "``ros2 param delete``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Using-ros2-param.rst:126
msgid ""
"This command will remove a parameter from a particular node. However, note "
"that this can only remove dynamic parameters (not declared parameters). See :"
"doc:`the concept document <../../About-Parameters>` for more information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Using-ros2-param.rst:130
msgid "$ ros2 param delete /my_node my_string"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Using-ros2-param.rst:135
msgid "``ros2 param describe``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Using-ros2-param.rst:137
msgid ""
"This command will provide a textual description of a particular parameter on "
"a particular node:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Using-ros2-param.rst:139
msgid "$ ros2 param describe /my_node use_sim_time"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Using-ros2-param.rst:144
msgid "``ros2 param dump``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Using-ros2-param.rst:146
msgid ""
"This command will print out all of the parameters on a particular node in a "
"YAML file format. The output of this command can then be used to re-run the "
"node with the same parameters later:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Using-ros2-param.rst:149
msgid "$ ros2 param dump /my_node"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Using-ros2-param.rst:154
msgid "``ros2 param load``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Using-ros2-param.rst:156
msgid ""
"This command will load the values of the parameters from a YAML file into a "
"particular node. That is, this command can reload values at runtime that "
"were dumped out by ``ros2 param dump``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Using-ros2-param.rst:159
msgid "$ ros2 param load /my_node my_node.yaml"
msgstr ""
